WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.160
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:03.816
- I can bench press 445 pounds.

00:00:03.816 --> 00:00:06.149
I can flip a 270 pound tire.

00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:11.246
I can do handstand push
ups, and I can climb a rope.

00:00:11.246 --> 00:00:13.486
And I can look damned good doing it.

00:00:13.486 --> 00:00:16.069
(upbeat music)

00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:22.991
I'm Zack Ruhl, an adaptive
crossfitter and a powerlifter.

00:00:22.991 --> 00:00:24.949
I was born with a deformity,

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:28.119
and pretty much my legs
looked real messed up,

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:29.987
so I would never be able to walk

00:00:29.987 --> 00:00:31.859
using them so they made a decision

00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:33.365
to get them amputated.

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:35.763
I've been an amputee, a double amputee,

00:00:35.763 --> 00:00:37.930
since I was two years old.

00:00:40.558 --> 00:00:41.831
(peaceful music)

00:00:41.831 --> 00:00:44.597
My relationship with fitness
started out in high school.

00:00:44.597 --> 00:00:46.956
I just started lifting
weights like anybody else,

00:00:46.956 --> 00:00:49.602
and I always did it for
appearance at first.

00:00:49.602 --> 00:00:50.988
If I'm just going to be a torso,

00:00:50.988 --> 00:00:53.625
I'm going to be one
damn looking good torso.

00:00:53.625 --> 00:00:55.250
And then it just took over my life.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.413
Like, I wanted to know
everything there is to know

00:00:57.413 --> 00:00:59.609
about the anatomy, the human body,

00:00:59.609 --> 00:01:02.570
how to get stronger, what
creates muscle growth.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.320
Like, I was a sponge.

00:01:05.174 --> 00:01:08.879
I've been told I can't bench
press more than 400 pounds.

00:01:08.879 --> 00:01:10.181
My ass.

00:01:10.181 --> 00:01:13.310
I've been told I wouldn't
have a gym of my own.

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.220
My biggest motivation in life is people

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.887
telling me I can't do something.

00:01:19.082 --> 00:01:21.499
(rock music)

00:01:22.541 --> 00:01:25.511
I offer free classes or
free personal training

00:01:25.511 --> 00:01:29.215
to adaptive athletes or
people with disabilities,

00:01:29.215 --> 00:01:31.818
so, I have a girl with cerebral palsy,

00:01:31.818 --> 00:01:34.990
I have a girl that has
a spinal cord injury,

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:37.356
and I have another quadruple amputee

00:01:37.356 --> 00:01:40.080
that I'm personal training right now.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.280
Crossfit has done so much for my life,

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.928
and I feel like I just
want to pass that on,

00:01:44.928 --> 00:01:46.760
and show everybody that it is possible,

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.593
you can work past disabilities,

00:01:48.593 --> 00:01:49.936
and whatever your goals are,

00:01:49.936 --> 00:01:51.647
especially fitness-wise,
you can meet them,

00:01:51.647 --> 00:01:53.512
it's just going to be a
little bit different route

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:55.259
than somebody else.

00:01:55.259 --> 00:01:57.676
(rock music)

